{"name":"Pound Cake","hex":"#fdf1c3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pound cake","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dense yellow cake, the traditional recipe for which consists of equal quantities (nominally one pound) of butter, eggs, flour, and sugar.","A term of attraction or desire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pound_cake"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pound Cake speech","blocks":[{"text":"The Pound Cake speech was given by Bill Cosby on May 17, 2004, during an NAACP Legal Defense Fund awards ceremony in Washington, D.C., to commemorate the 50th anniversary of the Brown v. Board of Education Supreme Court decision."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/BillCosby.jpg/330px-BillCosby.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pound_Cake_speech","wikidata":"Q16933378"},{"title":"Pound Cake / Paris Morton Music 2","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pound Cake / Paris Morton Music 2\" is a song by Canadian rapper Drake from his third studio album Nothing Was the Same released in 2013. The track consists of two songs, \"Pound Cake\" featuring a guest appearance by Jay-Z, and \"Paris Morton Music 2\", a sequel to \"Paris Morton Music\". The track serves as the outro to the standard edition of Nothing Was the Same."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pound_Cake_%2F_Paris_Morton_Music_2","wikidata":"Q17065014"},{"title":"Pound cake","blocks":[{"text":"Pound cake is a type of cake traditionally made with a pound of butter. Pound cakes are generally baked in either a loaf pan or a Bundt mould. They are sometimes served either dusted with powdered sugar, lightly glazed with syrup, with a coat of icing, or with whipped cream and fruit. Although the recipe was first recorded in England, the British rarely use the term instead calling them a traditional sponge cake or creamed sponge, while Australians use the term butter cake."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/Pound_cake_2.jpg/330px-Pound_cake_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pound_cake","wikidata":"Q29443"},{"title":"Cake","blocks":[{"text":"Cake is a baker's confectionery made by combining flour with a liquid, a fat or both, and usually with a leavening agent. Cakes are usually baked, but can be griddled. In their oldest forms, cakes were modifications of bread, but cakes now cover a wide range of preparations that can be simple or elaborate and which share features with other desserts such as pastries, meringues, custards, and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Pound_layer_cake.jpg/330px-Pound_layer_cake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cake","wikidata":"Q13276"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Jay-Z_7.jpg/500px-Jay-Z_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Jay-Z_7.jpg/500px-Jay-Z_7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jay-Z (pictured) is featured on “Pound Cake”. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJay-Z_7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Pound_cake%2C_September_2007_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pound_cake%2C_September_2007_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Pound_cake%2C_September_2007_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Pound_cake%2C_September_2007_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slices of pound cake","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APound_cake%2C_September_2007_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://